====================================================================================================
WIDTH IS ADDITIVE, NOT MULTIPLICATIVE
====================================================================================================
  V6 width = N + ceil(log2(M+1)) + 1 + n_scratch = N + log2(M+1) + 4.
  The excess is O(log M) ADDITIVE, so w6/N falls monotonically in N:
       N     w6/N
       2     5.00   H2 Molecule
       4     3.25   MaxCut N=4 (Opt=3.2)
       4     3.25   LiH Molecule
       4     3.25   Heisenberg N=4
       6     2.50   MaxCut N=6 (Opt=9.1)
       6     2.50   Heisenberg N=6
       8     2.25   Heisenberg N=8
  A reader who only sees Theta(G) will assume width parity. It is 5.00x
  at H2 and 2.25x at Heisenberg N=8, and tends to 1 - all three facts
  belong in the claim, not just the last one.

====================================================================================================
CLASSICAL WORK PER GRADIENT
====================================================================================================
  method                    classical                              at Heisenberg N=8
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift / AdamW   O(M) arithmetic                                       32
  Correct QNG               O(M) + O(L b^3) block inverse                       ~416
  SPSA                      O(M) arithmetic                                       32
  QLTO V6                   O(2^m_row) = O(M) decode                              64
  QSGD  (cited, adapted)    O(4^N) shadow matrices / layer                     65536
  Abbas Thm 9 (cited)       M * 2^Otilde(N) hypothesis state                    8192

  V6 carries NO exponential classical term. That is the column where the
  shadow-tomography methods lose outright, and it has never been claimed.

====================================================================================================
WHAT THIS LEDGER DOES NOT SAY
====================================================================================================
  Theta(G) circuits per gradient is a CONSTRUCTION-level fact: V6 issues G
  circuits whatever M is, at any problem size. It needs no measurement.
  What the 8-qubit suite establishes is the separate claim that V6 still
  CONVERGES competitively at that cost, and that is measured only to N=8.

  Two size-dependent caveats belong beside it, both already measured:
    v82  wide-ansatz regime, V6 variance exponent 1.94 vs p-shift 2.00 -
         at matched TOTAL SHOTS the advantage is circuits, not shots.
    v69  gradient error ~ T^(-1/3) for V6 against T^(-1/2) unbiased,
         fitted -0.742 / -0.759 against the predicted -2/3. The R-bias
         is the price and it does not vanish with more shots.
